                  <msItem>
                     <title>Consuetudinarium</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Formerly 122 leaves, now 39 fragments. Similar
                        to Cotton Faust. C.xii.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Smith's (1696) title is "Liber ordinis Ecclesie
                        Sancti Augustini Cant.: h. e. de disciplina consuetudinibus, sacris ritibus
                        et servitiis in festis anni diebus".</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Cf. E. Maunde Thompson, Customary of St
                        Augustine's, Canterbury..., HBS 2, p. xiii.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">A copy, due to Augustine Baker (who signs at
                        Cambrai in 1627), of at least a great part of the MS. is in Jesus Coll.
                        Oxford, 75 (fols. 329r--375v). It is headed (fol. 329r) "Liber ordinis de
                        Librario sancti augustini Cantuarie de adquisicione fratris Iohannis
                        Massyngham" (? a script facs.).</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
